flowchart TB
    subgraph CLI["`**CLI — main user interface**`"]
    C_init ~~~ C_ds

        direction TB
        C_init["`**init**
create working example and folders`"]
        C_ds["`**dataset from-csv / generate**
build the test set from scratch or from provided file`"]
        C_ev["`**evals new / validate** 
define evaluation criteria and scoring`"]
        C_mod["`**models list / ping**
check LLM providers reachable`"]
        C_run["`**run compare**
★ run the experiment`"]
        C_an["`**analyze**
compute comparison statistics`"]
        C_pow["`**power**
sample-size planning based on small test or estimates`"]
        C_rev["`**calibrate**
review judge decisions vs. human judgment (bias + agreement)`"]
    end

    DATA[/"dataset.jsonl"/]
    SPECS[/"eval specs
(eval.yaml + prompt.md)"/]

    subgraph CORE["core run loop (run compare)"]
        RC["runner
sweep model × record"]
        TASKS["`**Tasks**
produce output per record`"]
        MODELS["`**Models**
6 backends in provider registry
Supports: mock, ollama, openai, anthropic, bedrock, mantle`"]
        EVALS["`**Evals + Scoring**
LLM judge, programmatic, or ground-truth options`"]
    end

    STORE[("results.jsonl / .csv")]
    REVIEW[("review.jsonl")]
    ANALYSIS["`**Analysis**
Includes paired stats (Friedman, Wilcoxon, Cohen's d, TOST)
and mixed effects model
Renders report and plots`"]

    %% CLI commands each drive a different stage
    C_ds --> DATA
    C_ev --> SPECS
    C_mod -.probe.-> MODELS
    C_run ==> RC
    C_an --> ANALYSIS
    C_pow --> ANALYSIS
    STORE --> C_rev
    C_rev --> REVIEW
    C_init -.scaffold.-> DATA
    C_init -.scaffold.-> SPECS
    %% the run loop itself
    DATA --> RC
    SPECS --> EVALS
    RC --> TASKS --> MODELS
    RC --> EVALS
    EVALS -->|judge model| MODELS
    RC --> STORE --> ANALYSIS
